{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 31, :comments ["<b>Or a son or a daughter.</b> Both are Israelites, for it is written after it, \"if the slave\" (v. 32), and HaShem placed a punishment upon the owner of the ox, for it is grievous in His eyes that an animal kill a person created in the image of Elohim; therefore the ox is stoned."], :book :exodus, :voice :ibn-ezra, :lang :en, :chapter 21, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [["Piotrkow, 1907-1911" "https://www.nli.org.il/he/books/NNL_ALEPH990020973480205171/NLI"]], :timestamp "2026-07-09T18:37:11.851503663Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}